    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0250" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg134"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/913B.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Ambassador
                        to France</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-27T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1912—2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Refer to Department’s telegrams May 17, 3 p.m., and May 24, 2 p.m. Is there
                    anything to report as to the attitude of the Government to which you are
                    accredited?</p>
                <p>Repeat to embassies at London and Berlin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
